cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "calcinet"
abstract: >-
  A two-stage pipeline for estimating directed, signed neuronal connectivity
  from calcium imaging data. The first stage recovers a continuous spike proxy
  from fluorescence traces; the second fits a linear vector-autoregressive model
  to that proxy to estimate a directed connectivity matrix. The package provides
  chunked, out-of-core solvers that scale to networks of tens of thousands of
  neurons on CPU or GPU, together with provenance capture and a run ledger for
  reproducible experiments.
